# compare_integers — integer comparison operations
# (README §10.6). Tests less-than, equal, greater-than on Int64.

CompareIntegers is project
CompareIntegers module examplesCompareIntegers
CompareIntegers target console
CompareIntegers entry main

examplesCompareIntegers is module
examplesCompareIntegers path examples.compareIntegers
examplesCompareIntegers exports main
examplesCompareIntegers purpose "Demonstrate integer comparison operations"
examplesCompareIntegers invariant "10 < 20 is true"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Compare two integers and print result"
main invariant "10 < 20 evaluates to 1 (true)"

main let left immutable Int64 10
main let right immutable Int64 20
main let trueValue immutable Int64 1
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0

main do printComparisonResult
main return okCode

printComparisonResult is call
printComparisonResult in main
printComparisonResult invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printComparisonResult arg value Int64 trueValue
